{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>They go up the mountains</b> — and the meaning of \"אל מקום\" is that which he mentioned after it — \"גבול\" — he mentioned בל ישובון — as a sign, for at first the earth was covered with water, and by the will of HaShem, the wind pressed against the water, and the dry land appeared, after the light was created, which was the essence, as I explained in the account of Genesis."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:09.056655062Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}